hypertok

This project descends from gigatoken by Marcel Rød, distributed under the MIT License in LICENSE.
hypertok is an independent project. It is not an official gigatoken binding and is not affiliated
with or endorsed by Marcel Rød or the gigatoken project.

The overlap-and-verify mechanism follows LoPT, arXiv:2511.04952, Theorem 4.1, by C. Xu.

The compact vocabulary direction is credited to kitoken and its .kit format, distributed under
the BSD 2-Clause License. OpenAI tiktoken, SentencePiece, mistral-common, PtrHash, CHD, BBHash,
FMPH, the BPE boundary work of Berglund and van der Merwe, minbpe, and rustbpe informed the
documented prior-art analysis.

Vocabulary packages carry their own source license and notice files. Those terms apply in addition
to this repository's license when a vocabulary package is redistributed.

The browser demo bundles these tokenizer implementations for local comparison:

- js-tiktoken 1.0.21, from https://github.com/dqbd/tiktoken, under the MIT License.
- gpt-tokenizer 3.4.0, copyright 2023-2024 Bazyli Brzoska, under the MIT License.
- @dqbd/tiktoken 1.0.21, from https://github.com/dqbd/tiktoken, under the MIT License.
- @huggingface/tokenizers 0.1.3, copyright Hugging Face, under the Apache License 2.0.

The demo bundles Martian Mono SemiExpanded Regular, version 1.000, copyright 2020 The Martian
Mono Project Authors (https://github.com/evilmartians/mono), under the SIL Open Font License 1.1.
The font carries its license and copyright metadata.

